# SLA tracking

This system tracks production performance against partner SLAs in real time, so a partner heading for a breach is visible before it happens. Evaluation runs on every read from outage records and contract terms; the only persisted state is alert deduplication.

Every partner is tracking-only today. There are no SLA terms anywhere in the system, and no status, target, or penalty figure may be invented or defaulted.

Dashboard and alerts must call the same evaluation function. Never write a second implementation of the maths.

Every route handler and server component sets `export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic'` and fetches with `no-store`. Next.js caches by default, and a stale evaluation fails invisibly by showing plausible wrong numbers.
